# Everything the build does not need. Keeping .next out matters most: copying a
# host build into the image would ship a build made with the wrong env.
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
.git
.gitignore
*.log
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
docs
infra
wordpress
README.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude
.vscode
.idea
*.tsbuildinfo

# Mock fixtures. 252 KB of placeholder cover art that `public/` would otherwise
# publish at /mag/mock/covers/*.jpg — publicly reachable and crawlable on the
# production domain, from an image that never runs the mock: the container sets
# USE_MOCK=false and /mag/health confirms `source: "wpgraphql"`.
#
# Excluded rather than robots-disallowed, because a robots rule is a request not
# to index something that is still being served. Not shipping the bytes is the
# stronger statement and the smaller image.
#
# The consequence, stated so it is not a surprise: an image built from this
# Dockerfile CANNOT serve the mock's artwork. Mock development runs `next dev`
# from the repo, where public/mock is present. If a mock-backed container is
# ever wanted, this line has to come out deliberately.
public/mock
